# UBSan reports left alone on purpose, for tools/run_harnesses.sh SANITIZE=1.
#
# The EEL2 (Liveprog) interpreter is upstream WDL code. It packs pointers into
# its bytecode at whatever offset comes next and keeps its float stack pointer
# one before the array while empty. Both are undefined by the letter of C but
# deliberate, and fine on the arm64 and x86 parts this runs on. Not ours to
# rewrite; anything else in the engine is still reported.
alignment:nseel-compiler.c
alignment:glue_port.h
bounds:glue_port.h
pointer-overflow:glue_port.h
